{
  "_comment": [
    "Hermes memory (mem0 OSS). Two things here were silently fatal once:",
    "1) vector_store used 'path' (embedded qdrant) — the client locks that folder, so the",
    "   second process to open it dies with 'already accessed by another instance' and mem0",
    "   never initializes. Use host+port against hermes-qdrant.service instead.",
    "2) 'https': false is MANDATORY — qdrant-client silently switches to HTTPS as soon as",
    "   api_key is set, and a plain-HTTP server then fails with SSL: WRONG_VERSION_NUMBER.",
    "Also keep the llm model current: a retired model id (e.g. gemini-2.5-flash on a new",
    "key) returns 404 and every extraction fails while the store looks healthy.",
    "chmod 600 — this file holds the Qdrant API key."
  ],
  "mode": "oss",
  "agent_id": "hermes",
  "oss": {
    "llm": {
      "provider": "openai",
      "config": {
        "model": "gemini-flash-latest",
        "openai_base_url": "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/"
      }
    },
    "embedder": {
      "provider": "openai",
      "config": {
        "model": "gemini-embedding-001",
        "embedding_dims": 3072,
        "openai_base_url": "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/"
      }
    },
    "vector_store": {
      "provider": "qdrant",
      "config": {
        "collection_name": "hermes_mem0",
        "host": "127.0.0.1",
        "port": 6343,
        "api_key": "SAME_KEY_AS_qdrant.env",
        "https": false
      }
    }
  }
}
